{
  "dom_id": "step-4226",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "A **perfect square trinomial** is a three-term expression that is the result of squaring a binomial.\n\nFor example, the expression\n\n$$\nx^2 + 6x + 9\n$$\n\nis a perfect square trinomial because it is the result of squaring the binomial $(x+3)$, as shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+6x+9 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo factor a perfect square trinomial, we have to figure out what binomial it is the square of. We can often do this by relating the perfect square trinomial to the **square of a sum**:\n\n$$\nx^2 + {\\color{red}2}  {\\color{blue}a}x + {\\color{blue}a}^2 = (x + {\\color{blue}a})^2\n$$\n\n \n\nTo illustrate, let's factor the expression $x^2+6x+9$ using the square of sum formula. We perform the following steps:\n\n1\\. Write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n3\\. Factor the trinomial using the \"square of a sum formula\". In this case, we have ${\\color{blue}{a}}={\\color{blue}{3}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nThis method works *only* when the trinomial is a perfect square! It will *not* work for every trinomial. We will learn more general methods in the future.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-4226\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"4226\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"1596\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-4226\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-1\">Introduction</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"4226\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>A <strong>perfect square trinomial</strong> is a three-term expression that is the result of squaring a binomial.</p>\n<p>For example, the expression\n<span class=\"mjpage mjpage__block\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"11.719ex\" height=\"2.843ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.505ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -1006.6 5045.8 1223.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n\tx^2 + 6x + 9\n</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stro